Martin Read wrote:
> In short: Nice idea, but ultimately misguided.

I have to say that I find this comment- and others like it throughout
this thread (I'm not just pickingin you MR)- a little harsh.

While I accept that it's well worth discussing with the OP the balance
issues of removing glass from the game, we should also consider that
the OP may well be aware of this already. Perhaps the OP has devised
something extremely fiendish clever to address those issues, but
chooses not to tell us about it at this point. Even if s/he hasn't,
then it still might be nothing more than a programming exercise, or it
may be that the OP disagrees, and believes that removing glass without
making other changes would *not* be unbalancing. If that is the case,
then it's also worth remembering that the OP's opinion is as valid as
anyone else's, even if that anyone else has more experience of the game
or the source - and especially when it comes to coding carried out in
the privacy of the OP's own operating environment between consenting
compilers.

I also think we should also give the benefit of the doubt to the OP
that s/he would not post YAAP without specifying any patches/ mods that
the game was played under.

I'm not trying to tell anyone off or start a fight, but I just think
that some of the comments- while universally respectful, and
accompanied by helpful advice that does address the OP's question- were
a little less than encouraging. Nethack is open source for no reason
other than to allow people to make the changes that they want to make,
and that is one of its great strengths. The skill, knowledge and
patience to actually make changes to the nethack code are rare
commodities, and we should be doing everything we can to support and
nurture those few people who take an interest in developping them.

Perhaps I'm over-reacting. Everyone please try to read this post in the
friendly and constructive spirit in which I (tried to) write it.

